  "decision": "Carry-gated execution reduced risky-path exposure and improved mean p=0.05 expected discounted return over the source actor by 0.002876 on the predefined PACK TEST panel, with positive differences in four of five seeds. It simultaneously lowered fixed-kernel success from 100% to 98.75%, and its p=0.05 advantage over adapted-only execution was positive in only one of five seeds. The manual gate is therefore a risk-reducing but sometimes task-damaging policy composition, not a rule that preserves normal performance.",
